{"path":"utility/optional/hash","title":"std::hash<std::optional>","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>hash<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">&lt;std::optional&gt;</span>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/hash","section":"utility","kind":"page","summary":"The template specialization of std::hash for the std::optional class allows users to obtain hashes of the values contained in optional objects.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/optional\">&lt;optional&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx17\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> hash<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/optional\"><span class=\"kw1082\">std::<span class=\"me2\">optional</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The template specialization of <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/hash\">std::hash</a></span> for the <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/optional\">std::optional</a></span> class allows users to obtain hashes of the values contained in <code>optional</code> objects.\n</p><p>The specialization <code class=\"t-c\"><code>std::hash</code><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/optional\"><span class=\"kw1082\">std::<span class=\"me2\">optional</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span></span></code> is enabled (see <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/hash\">std::hash</a></span>) if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/hash\"><span class=\"kw1132\">std::<span class=\"me2\">hash</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/remove_cv\"><span class=\"kw603\">std::<span class=\"me2\">remove_const_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span></span></code> is enabled, and is disabled otherwise.\n</p><p>When enabled, for an object <code>o</code> of type <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/optional\"><span class=\"kw1082\">std::<span class=\"me2\">optional</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code> that contains a value, <code class=\"t-c\"><code>std::hash</code><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/optional\"><span class=\"kw1082\">std::<span class=\"me2\">optional</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>o<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> evaluates to the same value as <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/hash\"><span class=\"kw1132\">std::<span class=\"me2\">hash</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/remove_cv\"><span class=\"kw603\">std::<span class=\"me2\">remove_const_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>o<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>. For an optional that does not contain a value, the hash is unspecified.\n</p><p>The member functions of this specialization are not guaranteed to be noexcept because the hash of the underlying type might throw.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Template_parameters\">Template parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> T\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the type of the value contained in <code>optional</code> object\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;optional&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;string&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;unordered_set&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw1\">using</span> <span class=\"kw1\">namespace</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">literals</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">using</span> OptStr <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/optional\"><span class=\"kw1082\">std::<span class=\"me2\">optional</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// hash&lt;optional&gt; makes it possible to use unordered_set</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/unordered_set\"><span class=\"kw1297\">std::<span class=\"me2\">unordered_set</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>OptStr<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> s <span class=\"sy1\">=</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"st0\">\"ABC\"</span>s, <span class=\"st0\">\"abc\"</span>s, <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/optional/nullopt\"><span class=\"kw1086\">std::<span class=\"me2\">nullopt</span></span></a>, <span class=\"st0\">\"def\"</span>s\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> o <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> s<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> o.<span class=\"me1\">value_or</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"(null)\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\t</span>'</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/hash\"><span class=\"kw1132\">std::<span class=\"me2\">hash</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>OptStr<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>o<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>def     11697390762615875584\n(null)  18446744073709548283\nabc     3663726644998027833\nABC     11746482041453314842</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/hash\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>hash</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  hash function object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Template parameters","id":"Template_parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"utility","title":"Utility library"},{"path":"utility/optional","title":"std::optional"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::hash<std::optional>","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++17. The template specialization of std::hash for the std::optional class allows users to obtain hashes of the values…"},{"label":"Template parameters","note":"T"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"hash","note":"hash function object"}]}]},"standards":["C++11","C++17"],"wordCount":185,"codeBlockCount":2}
